WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.430
- Well, Bindi and Chandler,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.710
there's no segue for this,

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.590
from that sadness that
we just talked about,

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.910
but congrats on the marriage.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.490
So what was it like, you know,

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.706
getting married in the
middle of a pandemic?

00:00:12.706 --> 00:00:14.240
- [Bindi] Thank you.
- Thank you, yeah.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.073
- [Robert] So exciting.

00:00:15.073 --> 00:00:15.971
- [Bindi] 2020 was a wild year.

00:00:15.971 --> 00:00:16.804
- Holy moly.

00:00:16.804 --> 00:00:18.590
It was crazy because Australia Zoo

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.520
was actually temporarily closed

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.400
for a period of time during the pandemic.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.980
So we got married,

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.830
and then our honeymoon was
taking care of 1200 animals

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.740
with no guests coming in.
- Yeah.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.460
So it was a wild time.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.293
- It was really crazy.

00:00:31.293 --> 00:00:32.126
And then, you know,

00:00:32.126 --> 00:00:35.060
you always plan your
wedding with lots of guests.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.355
And I think it was just
us and the animals.

00:00:39.355 --> 00:00:40.480
- That was pretty much it, yep.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.530
- Very small, but, you know,
it was really, really special

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.210
and we're just glad to be married

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.740
and glad to be able to be husband and wife

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.740
while taking on this wild
2020 and new 2021, so.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:53.940
- It's a silver lining.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.760
You gotta grab every silver lining you can

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:57.779
when times are tough.
- That's it exactly.

00:00:57.779 --> 00:00:58.612
- [Robert] For sure.
- It's true.

00:00:58.612 --> 00:00:59.872
- I was just about to say the same thing.

00:00:59.872 --> 00:01:01.630
It is a beautiful silver lining.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.860
And actually I think it's beautiful

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.210
that you had all these animals around

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.043
like while you're getting married.

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:07.130
I think it's a really beautiful thing

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:10.250
that it's a part of what
your family, you know,

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.790
what you're the vessel for
and your purpose is in life.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.160
And to have that a part of your wedding,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.020
that's actually really cool.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.740
Well, Robert, how did it feel
to walk Bindi down the aisle?

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.050
- Ah, it was amazing.

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.460
It was definitely just

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.810
one of the most incredible
moments of my entire life.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.690
I felt so honored when
Bindi first asked me

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.440
to walk her down the aisle.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.700
And then when everything
was coming down to the wire

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:33.840
and we were planning this wedding,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.440
it was really, really hard

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.980
because, of course, there were no guests.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.080
It was just a little bit chaotic,

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.240
but at the end of the
day, it all came together,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.610
and it was just the most
beautiful moment ever.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:47.740
I think for me, I was incredibly
emotional at the same time.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.960
Not only being so proud for
Bindi, it's such a happy day,

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.020
but also kinda thinking, you know,

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.260
how much I wish that
dad could've been there,

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.100
and that was his job to
walk her down the aisle,

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.740
but I felt very honored to be there,

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.230
I guess, sort of on his behalf.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.450
And I think we definitely
felt him on the day,

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.210
and yeah, it was incredibly emotional,

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.530
but just so special.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.780
I'll never, ever forget
that, it was amazing.

